{{Quote|Molded from high-impact synthetic polymers. This sleek, stark white faceless armor both reduces mass manufacturing costs and ensures the wearer is highly visible on almost every battlefield, bravely drawing enemy fire away from considerably more costly vehicular assets.|[[Armory]] Description}}

'''BFM-77 Reformer''' is a set of [[medium armor]] in ''[[Helldivers 2]]''.

== Acquisition ==
Both the body armor and [[helmet]] can be purchased from the Superstore for {{Currency|SC|250|notext}} and {{Currency|SC|125}} respectively.

== Trivia ==
* The Reformer bears a resemblance to the armor worn by [https://starwars.fandom.com/wiki/Imperial_Remnant_AT-RT_Driver Imperial Remnant AT-RT Drivers] from the ''Star Wars'' franchise, first appearing in [https://starwars.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars:_The_Mandalorian_and_Grogu ''The Mandalorian And Grogu (2026)''].
** Additionally, the numeric designation of BFM-'''77''' may be in reference to original release date of ''Star Wars'', May 25, 1977.

